le\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Static triangles do exist among the target nodes (one per node, e.g. 220-306-1554 and 34-452-617), but binning participant activity at the 800-unit closure tolerance shows their events are isolated singletons separated by roughly 800-3200 time units. No wedge is followed by its closing interaction within 800 units, so the triads are aggregation artifacts of a 12k-wide window rather than a genuine closure wave. Volume (2746 events, repeat ratio 0.008) and per-node popularity (2-5 events each) are both too thin to support a wave independently.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 19744, "total_output_tokens": 4205, "total_tokens": 23949, "total_latency_ms": 61316, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}